## Summary

K-Means partitions vector spaces by minimizing squared Euclidean distance from centroids. K-Means++ mitigates initialization sensitivity, while K-Medoids replaces cluster means with actual medoid observations to improve outlier robustness [@macqueen1967; @arthur2007; @kaufman1990].

